@using Viman.Models

@{
    ViewBag.PageName = "home";
    Layout = "~/Views/Shared/_Layout.cshtml";



}

@section metatags{
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <link rel="icon" type="image/x-icon" href="~/images/favicon.ico">

    <title>Faresradar-Privacy Policy</title>

}

<link rel="stylesheet" href="~/css1/index.css">

<div class="hero">
    <h1 style="color:white!important">Privacy Policy</h1>
</div>
    

<div class="container1">
    <div class="row1">
        <div class="column">
            <p>Your privacy is important to us at FARESRADAR. We will protect any personal information that you give to us. This privacy policy provides information about how we obtain, utilise, disclose, and secure information that you supply to us using our travel comparison platform. Using or accessing our site entails that you have accepted the practices outlined in this policy.</p>

            <h2>The Information That We Gather</h2>
            <p>The kind of information that we can collect when you use our site includes:</p>

            <h3>Personal Information</h3>
            <p>Name, email address, or other contact information in case we call you directly.</p>

            <h3>Non-Personal Information</h3>
            <p>Browser, operating system, type of device, IP address, place, the number of pages, duration, search activities, and website or ad to get the reference.</p>

            <h3>Cookies and Tracking Techs</h3>
            <p>To recall preferences, study the performance of platforms, and increase user experience, we employ cookies and such. Cookies are controllable and can be set off in your browser.</p>

            <h2>Our Use of Your Information</h2>
            <p>FARESRADAR employs the data acquired to offer and enhance our comparator travel services, show appropriate flight, hotel, and car-hire proposals, monitor and track the trend of users to improve performance on platforms, handle customer care requests and answer questions of the users, present hometown promotions and deals, and prevent fraud or suspicious activity. Our personal information is not sold to third parties.</p>

            <h2>Third-Party Links and Partners</h2>
            <p>FARESRADAR is a travel comparison engine that shows the results of third-party travel providers. By clicking a link or booking button, you might be diverted to the site of a partner. The privacy policies of such third-party sites differ, and we are not responsible for their actions. We urge users to go through their privacy policies first when sharing any personal information on other websites.</p>

            <h2>Data Sharing</h2>
            <p>We can also give anonymised and aggregated information to our analysis providers or business partners to enhance our services. Personally identifiable information is never shared by us except when legally or regulatory-requested, to realise our terms and defend rights or safety, or upon consent of the users.</p>

            <h2>Data Security</h2>
            <p>To ensure that your data is not accessed, modified, or disclosed by unauthorised persons, we implement security standards used in the industry. No one can guarantee 100% protection, and we put reasonable protection in place.</p>

            <h2>Retention Policy of Data</h2>
            <p>FARESRADAR does not keep user information any longer than needed. Analysis data are allowed to be stored over extended durations to make the services run better and the reports more exact. When you have provided us with personal information, that data will only be kept as long as necessary to reply, or as long as the law may require. As soon as you no longer need it, your information will be deleted or anonymised in the best practices of the industry.</p>

            <h2>Your Rights and Choices</h2>
            <p>You are being provided the right to get copies of the information we have about you, ask for a correction or deletion of personal data, allow privacy settings of the browser to opt-out of cookies, and revoke the consent. To use these rights or demand that the data be removed, get in touch with us via email.</p>

            <h2>Children's Privacy</h2>
            <p>We do not knowingly and intentionally process or collect the information of children below the age of 13. In case we discover that we have gathered information about a child unconsciously, we will eliminate it at that moment.</p>

            <h2>Alteration to This Privacy Policy</h2>
            <p>We can revise this privacy policy as the technology warrants, as the laws change, or when the service is enhanced. The updated policy will be displayed on this page, along with the updated effective date. We also advise you to read this policy frequently so that you are updated on the protection of your data.</p>

            <h2>Analytics Tools Consumption</h2>
            <p>FARESRADAR employs analytics to appreciate the interactions of its users with its web pages better. These are simple tools to collect anonymised data about how you behave, such as the amount of time spent on the site, pages visited, and referral sources, to enable us to make performance and content more relevant.</p>

            <h2>Affiliate Links Use</h2>
            <p>FARESRADAR can use affiliate links in search results and other content. By clicking on these links and then paying for a transaction, you may help us receive a small but free commission. On our free-to-use comparison site, the links aid in supporting our services and are identified or promoted through trusted travel partners.</p>

            <h2>International Users</h2>
            <p>FARESRADAR has its operation base in the United States, and we also accept users worldwide. In case you are reading the site somewhere beyond the U.S., you should take into consideration that your data may be transferred, stored, and processed in the United States or other countries where we have our servers or our partners are situated.</p>

            <h2>Legal Grounds for Processing of Personal Data</h2>
            <p>Where users are based in jurisdictions requiring a legal basis for data processing, such as under GDPR, we process your data on the basis of consent, in which you say yes, reasonable interest to run and improve the site, adherence to a contract, such as supporting requests, or obeying the law as a legal requirement.</p>

            <h2>Third-party Widgets and Embedded Content</h2>
            <p>In our location, we can present embedded applications or objects such as Google Maps, price widgets, or hotel review plug-ins. Such tools can take data in terms of your engagement with the material. We do not govern how these third-party widgets manage your information.</p>

            <h2>Agreement with This Policy</h2>
            <p>This privacy policy comes into effect when you use our website. In case you are not in agreement with any severity of the policy, it is preferred that you avoid using the platform. To accept the changed terms, one will need to stick to the platform following the amendment of the policy.</p>

            <h2>Final Note</h2>
            <p>FARESRADAR is devoted to keeping your data safe and combines it with transparency, care, and respect. In the changing landscape of travel in a digital world, our practices will change as well, and your trust and safety will remain at their centre. All users should read this privacy policy and contact us with questions and concerns regularly. Thank you for trusting us, your travel comparison partner.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

